From 3f5af2810a3fd1f86316ff05588bdf030f808eeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Maddox <benwmaddox@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:54:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Unread as counts: a post writes the room and its poster,
 not every member

As in etch: rooms.posts_count counts the room's posts, memberships.seen_posts is the count a
member last saw, and a room is unread while the room's count is ahead. A post adds one to the
room (activity) and catches its poster up (their read state); presence and read catch a
member up. Rails set unread_at on every member's row that wasn't connected (the 60-second
connected rule is gone, as in etch). The columns are added at boot to a database without them,
carrying today's unread rooms over. The sidebar's direct-room fragment is also keyed by the
room's updated_at and its unread state, which a post now changes without touching the
membership.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
